chine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 13 of 296 ===\npresidential documents\n[3195-01]\nTitle 3—The President\nExecutive Order 12054 , • April 21,1978\nPresident's Commission on Foreign Language and International Studies\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution  \nand statutes of the United States of America, and in accordance with the  \nprovisions of the Federal Advisory Committee Act (5 U.S.C. App. I), it is  \nhereby ordered as follows l\nS e c t io n 1. Establishment, (a) There is hereby established the President’s  \nCommission on Foreign Language and International Studies, hereinafter re­\nferred to as the Commission.\n(b) The Commission shall consist of not more than twenty-five members  \nto be appointed by the President, one of whom shall be designated by the  \nPresident to chair the Commission.\nSec. 2. Functions, (a) The Commission shall conduct such public hearings,  \ninquiries, and studies as may be necessary to make recommendations to the  \nPresident and the Secretary of Health, Education, and Welfare ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_12054.txt","sha256":"64cd46dccd58c984bca30fe1234c360ceee8ab324cf5c57debefc91564251891","source":{"line":1579,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6604fe06451c33e489ec9efa947d5f47c64387475a6d262169a609d6ae8f254f"}}]}
